by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-18T13:35:46Z

My `%kernel.share_dir%/assets` suggestion was wrong: `Kernel::getShareDir()` returns `getCacheDir()` unless `APP_SHARE_DIR` is set, so `cache:clear` wipes it just like the build dir. I probed all four layouts:

| `metadata_dir` | after `cache:clear` |
| --- | --- |
| `%kernel.share_dir%/assets`, default layout | gone |
| `%kernel.share_dir%/assets`, separate `var/build` | gone |
| `APP_SHARE_DIR=var/share` | survives |
| unset (public assets dir, today's default) | survives |

And it fails silently: the manifest is absent, `getPublicPath()` still resolves, the import map is just rebuilt from source on every request. `cache:clear` renames both the cache dir and the build dir aside and replaces the build dir with the warmup copy, so only what a warmer regenerates survives. `%kernel.build_dir%` has the same problem, which is what you had spotted for the original name.

So there is no good default to promise for 9.0 right now, and picking one freezes it into the deprecation message. I dropped the deprecation and kept the option: the feature is useful on its own, people who care can set it today, and we can deprecate later once we have somewhere sensible to point at (a directory `cache:clear` never manages, or `share_dir` plus a warmer that recompiles).

What I changed on top of your branch:

- removed the deprecation, the UPGRADE entry and the `symfony/deprecation-contracts` requirement (it was the only `trigger_deprecation()` in the component)
- the two legacy tests are now plain tests, and dropped the `IgnoreDeprecations` import they orphaned
- added `cannotBeEmpty()`: `metadata_dir: ''` used to be accepted and gave a CWD-relative path
- `abstract_arg('public assets directory')` -> `'metadata directory'`, since it is not the public dir any more
- fixtures use `%kernel.project_dir%/var/assets` instead of `share_dir`, so we are not advertising the location that does not survive
- reverted the `BundlePaths` config change, which only existed to silence the deprecation
- squashed, rebased, retitled to `[AssetMapper]`

@GromNaN your approval predates the rebase, worth a fresh look.
